    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194-a3">

                <pb facs="0372" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg332"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 24, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to your letter of October
                    last relative to some discharged convicts from Newfoundland who received public
                    aid to quit the colony, and made use of that aid to proceed to the United
                    States, I have the honor to inform you that a despatch has been received <pb
                        facs="0373" n="333" xml:id="pg333"/> from the governor of Newfoundland
                    stating that he will do his best to prevent, so far as depends upon the
                    government, the recurrence of any similar grounds of complaint.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
